    {
      "id": "E3",
      "source": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "field": "hanzi.etymology_notes[2]",
      "text": "冒也。冒地而生。東方之行。从屮，下象其根。凡木之屬皆从木。",
      "record_character": "木",
      "kind": "imported_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "id": "E4",
      "source": "wiktionary",
      "field": "hanzi.etymology_notes[3]",
      "text": "Pictogram (象形) – a tree: branches on top, roots on the bottom (more visible in earlier forms).\nSee also 本, 未, and 末.\nNo known cognate exists. It can perhaps be compared with Proto-Karen *məŋᴮ (“trunk (of a tree); firewood”) (Starostin) or Proto-Lolo-Burmese *ʔmuk (“stump (of a tree)”) (Schuessler, 2007).\nThe common Sino-Tibetan root for “tree; wood” is *siŋ ~ sik, represented by 薪 (OC *siŋ, “firewood”).",
      "record_character": "木",
      "kind": "imported_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "id": "E5",
      "source": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "field": "hanzi.shuowen.explanation",
      "text": "冒也。冒地而生。東方之行。从屮，下象其根。凡木之屬皆从木。",
      "record_character": "木",
